issues.body:
The item list will get long. Please add `limit` and `offset` query parameters to `GET /items`:

- `limit` defaults to 50, must be between 1 and 200 (422 otherwise);
- `offset` defaults to 0 and can't be negative (422);
- the body stays a plain JSON list, so existing clients don't break;
- add an `X-Total-Count` response header with the number of items matching the filters before paging.

Paging applies after filtering and sorting.

Two people edited the same item at once and one change silently disappeared. Let's add optimistic concurrency:

- each item gets a `version` number, starting at 1 and going up by one on every change (PATCH or adjust);
- `GET /items/{sku}` returns an `ETag` header holding the version;
- `PATCH` and `adjust` accept an `If-Match` header; if it's present and doesn't match the current version, return 412 and change nothing;
- without `If-Match` they behave as now, so existing clients keep working.

The version check and the change must happen together, not as a separate read then write.
